{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find current Prodigi Print API v4 documentation and product catalog details for a black unisex or men's T-shirt available via Prodigi sandbox. I need exact SKU patterns per size S/M/L/XL, required order payload fields, print area name, supported asset file types/URL requirements, and sandbox order behavior. Prefer Prodigi official sources and include source URLs."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find current Prodigi Print API v4 documentation and product catalog details for a black unisex or men's T-shirt available via Prodigi sandbox. I need exact SKU patterns per size S/M/L/XL, required order payload fields, print area name, supported asset file types/URL requirements, and sandbox order behavior. Prefer Prodigi official sources and include source URLs."},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Prodigi Print API v4 Documentation and Product Catalog Details for Black Unisex T-Shirts in Sandbox Environment\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nProdigi's Print API v4 offers comprehensive documentation and a diverse product catalog, including black unisex T-shirts. The API provides detailed SKU patterns for various sizes, specifies required order payload fields, defines print area names, supports multiple asset file types, and outlines sandbox order behavior, facilitating seamless integration and testing for developers.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** Prodigi's unisex T-shirts are available in sizes S, M, L, and XL, each with specific SKU patterns.\n\n- **Finding 2:** The required order payload fields include `shippingMethod`, `recipient` details, and `items` with `sku`, `copies`, `sizing`, and `assets` containing `printArea` and `url`.\n\n- **Finding 3:** The primary print area for T-shirts is labeled as \"default,\" and the API supports asset file types such as PNG and PDF, with a preference for PNG due to its support for transparency.\n\n- **Finding 4:** In the sandbox environment, orders are not fulfilled or charged, allowing developers to test integrations without financial risk.\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: Prodigi Print API Documentation & Guides\n\n- **URL:** ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official documentation from Prodigi)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Prodigi Print API documentation provides comprehensive guides and references for integrating print-on-demand services. It includes information on API endpoints, order objects, and authentication methods. The documentation emphasizes the availability of both sandbox and live environments, allowing developers to test their integrations without incurring charges. The sandbox environment mirrors the live environment's features, ensuring consistency during testing.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Sandbox API URL: `https://api.sandbox.prodigi.com`\n\n- Live API URL: `https://api.prodigi.com`\n\n- Authentication requires an `X-API-Key` header.\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Sandbox is our testing environment. It will not fulfil your orders, and you will not be charged for using it.\"\n\n> \"Each request to our API requires the use of an authentication header: `X-API-Key`.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 2: Print API | FAQ | Prodigi\n\n- **URL:** ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/faq/print-api/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** FAQ\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official FAQ from Prodigi)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe FAQ section addresses common queries about the Prodigi Print API, including the differences between sandbox and live environments, API key management, and supported image file types. It clarifies that sandbox and live environments have separate API keys and that the sandbox environment is intended for testing without order fulfillment or charges. The FAQ also specifies that the API accepts high-quality JPG, PNG, or PDF files, with a preference for PNG due to its support for transparency.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Sandbox and live environments have different API keys.\n\n- Supported image file types: JPG, PNG, PDF.\n\n- Preference for PNG files for products requiring transparency.\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Sandbox API keys cannot be used on the Live API and vice versa.\"\n\n> \"We can work with a very wide variety of image file formats although our preference is for high-quality JPG, PNG or PDF files, depending on the product.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 3: Print on Demand Classic Unisex Custom T-Shirt - Print API, Drop shipping\n\n- **URL:** ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/products/mens-clothing/t-shirts/classic/unisex-t-shirt-non-branded/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Product Page\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official product information from Prodigi)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis product page details the classic unisex T-shirt available through Prodigi's print-on-demand service. The T-shirt is offered in multiple colors, including black, and is available in sizes S, M, L, and XL. The page specifies that the printing method used is direct to garment, and the materials include cotton and polyester. It also provides care instructions and emphasizes the use of water-based inks for printing.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Available sizes: S, M, L, XL.\n\n- Printing method: Direct to garment.\n\n- Materials: Cotton, Polyester.\n\n- File format requirements: PNG or PDF.\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"We accept jpg and png format images. For some products we may recommend one format over the other (e.g. apparel and device cases work best with png).\"\n\n> \"Printed using water based inks.\"\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n**Consensus Across Sources:**\n\n- The sandbox environment allows for testing without order fulfillment or charges. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- Supported asset file types include JPG, PNG, and PDF, with a preference for PNG for products requiring transparency. ([prodigi.com](https://www.pro